  "notes": "Chipmunk soul is a register decision before it is a harmony decision, and this model is authored that way. Because the source is sped up, the keys sit on the sharp side and the sample lands soprano-high — `melody.register` starts at 72, the highest in this batch, which is what leaves the wide mid-gap the research describes for the vocal. `motifPitchCount` is [5,7] because the loop is reassembled from about seven chops. Drums are mixed as loud as the loop, so `velocityTiers.main` is 90–102; the machine-gun 16th kick clusters are `densityPerBar` [4,7] with `walkingRunProb` 0.45 and `syncopation` 0.6. ⚠ The bass is `independent_riff`, and that is a reading of the research's own words — \"re-sequenced bass-guitar stabs used percussively\" is a played, moving part, not a held sub. The \"heavy sub on the downbeats\" it also names is carried by the kick layer, because this genre archetype has no 808 lane. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set: the melody instrument is a *voice*, and the harmony is whatever the source record did. The I–IV family at weight 2 is a REDUCTION of the researched I–IV–V, not a new claim. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium.",
